# PROJECT: UNIFIED HOSPITALITY & RECREATION BOOKING PLATFORM

## 1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a Senior Product Designer, UI/UX Architect, Full-Stack Developer, and SaaS Product Engineer.

Build a complete, polished, fully interactive, client-presentation-ready web application prototype for a business that operates three services under one brand:

1. Turf Booking
2. Resort Room Booking
3. Restaurant & Food Ordering

The system must have two main interfaces:

- Customer-facing website
- Unified Admin Dashboard

IMPORTANT: This is not a static design or a collection of screenshots. Build a working, navigable, interactive web application with realistic sample data, functional forms, booking flows, dashboards, filters, and management operations.

The prototype should be polished enough to demonstrate to a real business client and secure project approval.

---

# 2. CORE BUSINESS CONCEPT

One business operates three different services at one location.

Each service has its own customer experience and booking logic.

However, the business owner manages everything through ONE unified admin panel.

Core architecture:

- One business brand
- One customer website
- Three independent service modules
- One admin authentication system
- One unified admin dashboard
- One shared customer database
- One shared payment management system
- Independent booking and inventory management
- Combined analytics and reports

Do not create three separate websites or three separate admin panels.

---

# 3. TECHNOLOGY REQUIREMENTS

Build using:

- React
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Lucide React icons
- Modern reusable components
- React Router or equivalent routing
- Local state management
- LocalStorage persistence for demo data
- Responsive layouts

Use clean component architecture.

Organize code into reusable components, pages, layouts, and service-specific modules.

The prototype must run without requiring an external backend.

Use realistic mock data and simulate payment success.

All demo operations must work locally.

Do not require API keys or external credentials.

